<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104249" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τομ-εύς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έως</span>, ὁ, 
			Dor.
		 dat. pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τομέεσσι</span> (vv. ll.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τομέσι, τομεσσι</span>) <i><span class="en">
			Archim.
			<u>Spir.</u>
			25
		</span></i>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one that
				cuts, a carver,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				6.13
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. σίδηρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Max.
					277
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέλεκυς αὐχένος τ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Trag.Adesp.</u>
					412
				</span></i>
			; <i>divider,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ ἀόρατος τ.,</span> i. e. God, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.498
			</span></i>; as Adj., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ τ.
			λόγος</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				491
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>shoemaker's knife,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Alc.</u>
				1.129c
			</span></i>; <i>edge of a knife,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Eq.Mag.</u>
				2.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>forceps,</i>
			
				gloss on 
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τομεῖον</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				19.146
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τομεῖς, οἱ,</span>
			<i>cutting-teeth, incisors,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Anon.Lond.
				24.23
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Cels.
				8.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				2.754
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				2.91
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Gp.</u>
				16.1.13
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Simp.
				<u>in Cael.</u>
				664.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> Math.,
				<i>sector</i> of a circle, <i><span class="en">
				Euc.
				6.33
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hero
			</span></i>
			<i>*Deff.</i><i><span class="en">
				34
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. στερεός</span>
			<i>sector</i> of a sphere (intercepted by cone with vertex at
			centre), <i><span class="en">
				Archim.
				<u>Sph.</u>
			</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Sph.Cyl.</u>
				1
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Def.</u>
				5
			</span></i>; but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. ἐν τῇ
			ἐπιφανείᾳ,</span> i.e. surface included betw. two great
			circles and a circle cutting each at right angles, <i><span class="en">
				Papp.
				268.1
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
